    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Record growth, broken chart: ALAB slides 15% in AI-wide selloff",
               "technical":  "Trend: ALAB closed at $180.35 on 2026-11-20, far below all three EMAs (exponential moving averages, which weight recent prices more): EMA50 $264.77, EMA100 $278.88 and EMA200 $261.31. Price is about 31% under the 200-day line. The EMA50 has already slipped below the EMA100 and is now only about $3 above the EMA200. The medium-term uptrend is broken, and a bearish EMA50/200 cross is close. Momentum: MACD 12/26/9 (a trend-momentum gauge) is −24.19, exactly on its signal line, so the histogram is 0. Momentum is still deep in negative territory. Selling pressure had been easing, and Friday\u0027s drop tests that. RSI 14 (a 0–100 gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 33.04, near oversold but not there yet. Volatility: the Bollinger Bands (20-day, 2 standard deviations) are very wide, from $163.34 to $295.21. Price sits in the lower part, about $17 above the lower band. The stock is 64% below its 52-week high of $499.48, in the bottom fifth of the $97.89–$499.48 range. Volume was 7.92M shares, 1.44× the 20-day average, and the close was near the day\u0027s low of $176.78, so the selling had conviction. Support: the lower band near $163. Resistance: $203–206 (Friday\u0027s open and high), then the $229 mid-band.",
               "fundamental":  "The business is speeding up even as the stock falls. Q3 2026 results came out on 2026-11-03. Revenue was a record $584.9M, up 154% from a year earlier and 49% from the prior quarter. GAAP gross margin was 72.3% and non-GAAP EPS was $1.32. Q4 guidance of $730–750M is well above the roughly $656M analysts expected. Scorpio fabric switches are now the largest product family, running above $1B a year. That supports the move from retimers into higher-value switching, a key part of the moat. Two products extend reach to neoclouds and enterprises: the Orion rack-scale boards (available Q1 2027) and the expanded Hyve/TD SYNNEX deal. Weak spots: the top three end customers made up about 86% of 2025 revenue. The CFO also said the first Scorpio X platforms had finished much of their initial ramp, which sparked fears that growth will flatten.",
               "news":  [
                            "2026-11-03: Q3 revenue was $584.9M (+154% YoY), and non-GAAP EPS of $1.32 beat estimates. Q4 guidance is $730–750M with about 72% gross margin. The stock still fell 4.4% on 2026-11-04.",
                            "After earnings, the CFO said the first Scorpio X platforms had \u0027completed much of their initial deployment ramps.\u0027 That raised fears of a plateau. At BMO\u0027s conference in mid-November, management said Scorpio X should end 2026 well above a $1B yearly run rate. They also expect 2–3 more customers on top of the two hyperscalers already shipping.",
                            "2026-11-05: ALAB fell 19.6% in a chip-wide selloff after the 2026-11-03 midterm elections. New governors in Texas, Ohio and Georgia, all big data center states, have promised construction moratoriums. Every peer fell by double digits, and ALAB fell the most.",
                            "Analyst moves: UBS cut its price target to $290 from $300 on 2026-11-04. BMO started coverage at Outperform with a $375 target on 2026-11-06. The consensus rating is still Buy.",
                            "2026-11-16: Astera and Hyve Solutions (part of TD SYNNEX) expanded their partnership. Hyve will put Orion compute, fabric and link boards into its air-cooled Apex racks. The stock still fell 8.8% that day as 33 of 34 large chip stocks declined, then rebounded about 4.8% on 2026-11-17.",
                            "CEO Jitendra Mohan sold 96,089 shares in a transaction dated 2026-11-16, according to an insider-trading report.",
                            "2026-11-20: ALAB fell 14.77% with no company-specific news. It was a broad AI selloff: Nvidia and AMD each lost more than 13%, Anthropic fell 8.5% on its first full trading day, and Nvidia\u0027s leadership change and worries about interest rates weighed on the whole group."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The chart is in a clear downtrend. The stock is 64% below its June high, mostly because of market-wide moves rather than company news. That makes it a high-beta bet on AI mood: Nvidia\u0027s leadership turmoil, data center moratorium pledges, export-control scrutiny and rising rates can all keep pressure on it. Because so much revenue comes from a few customers, a pause at one hyperscaler would hurt. MACD is still deeply negative and RSI has not yet dropped below 30, so the selling may not be over. A break below about $163 would leave little support nearby.",
               "opportunity":  "The business and the share price are moving in opposite directions. The Q4 guide alone implies about $3B in yearly revenue, margins are holding near 72%, and management expects 2–3 new Scorpio X customers. The 2026-11-20 drop came with no bad news from the company itself. RSI near 33 and price close to the lower Bollinger band put the stock where past selloffs have sometimes paused. For long-term holders, the test is whether Q4 delivers $730–750M. If it does, the drop looks more like a sentiment problem than damage to the business.",
               "risks":  [
                             "AI-trade sentiment shock: Nvidia\u0027s leadership turmoil, money rotating into the Anthropic IPO and rising interest rates could squeeze valuations across the sector.",
                             "Policy risk: data center construction moratoriums promised in Texas, Ohio and Georgia, plus wider scrutiny of chip export controls.",
                             "Customer concentration: the top three end customers were about 86% of 2025 revenue.",
                             "Scorpio X growth could flatten after the first hyperscaler ramps, and Broadcom and Marvell compete in switching.",
                             "High volatility and valuation: about 22.6× trailing sales at the 2026-11-16 close, and moves of this size happened on about 20 trading days in the past year.",
                             "Insider selling: the CEO sold 96,089 shares on 2026-11-16."
                         ],
               "summary":  "ALAB fell 14.77% to $180.35 on 2026-11-20 on heavy volume, extending a slide that began after the 2026-11-03 earnings report. The chart is bearish: price is far below all three EMAs, MACD is deeply negative and RSI is near oversold. The company news is strong, though: record revenue of $584.9M, a Q4 guide of $730–750M and Scorpio switches running above $1B a year. The big drops on Nov 5, 16 and 20 hit the whole sector. The moat thesis looks intact; the risks are market sentiment and customer concentration, not the product."
